# WN22-DC-000320: Windows Server 2022 domain controllers must require LDAP access signing.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-dc-000320-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 domain controllers must require LDAP access signing.`
    description `Unsigned network traffic is susceptible to man-in-the-middle attacks, where an intruder captures packets between the server and the client and modifies them before forwarding them to the client. In the case of an LDAP server, this means that an attacker could cause a client to make decisions based on false records from the LDAP directory. The risk of an attacker pulling this off can be decreased by implementing strong physical security measures to protect the network infrastructure. Furthermore,`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,registry,medium,ksi-afr-ads,ksi-cna-mat,ksi-cna-uln,ksi-svc-snt`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-AFR-ADS,KSI:KSI-CNA-MAT,KSI:KSI-CNA-ULN,KSI:KSI-SVC-SNT,NIST-800-53:SC-8,NIST-800-53:SC-8(1)`
    control_objective `KSI-AFR-ADS,KSI-CNA-MAT,KSI-CNA-ULN,KSI-SVC-SNT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> Domain controller: LDAP server signing requirements to "Require signing".`

    component_id `comp-windows-registry`

    impl_KSI_AFR_ADS `Windows Server implements KSI-AFR-ADS by setting registry value 'LDAPServerIntegrity' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\NTDS\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_CNA_MAT `Windows Server implements KSI-CNA-MAT by setting registry value 'LDAPServerIntegrity' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\NTDS\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_CNA_ULN `Windows Server implements KSI-CNA-ULN by setting registry value 'LDAPServerIntegrity' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\NTDS\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_KSI_SVC_SNT `Windows Server implements KSI-SVC-SNT by setting registry value 'LDAPServerIntegrity' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\NTDS\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_SC_8 `Windows Server implements SC-8 by setting registry value 'LDAPServerIntegrity' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\NTDS\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`
    impl_SC_8_1 `Windows Server implements SC-8(1) by setting registry value 'LDAPServerIntegrity' under 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\NTDS\Parameters' to the STIG-mandated REG_DWORD value. The ESP scanner reads the value via the registry CTN and fails the policy if the key is absent or the value does not match the required setting. Remediation restores the configuration via Group Policy or direct registry edit per the STIG fix guidance.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        hive `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE`
        key `SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\NTDS\Parameters`
        name `LDAPServerIntegrity`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int = 2
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN registry
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
